-- title:
--   Constant for energy jumps of a single entry
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a heat-flow proof that the maximally truncated triangular Hilbert transform maps $L^3\times L^3$ to $L^{3/2}$. After a change of variables the problem becomes a cyclic trilinear form $\sum_{i,j,k}A^{(0)}_{ij}A^{(1)}_{jk}A^{(2)}_{ki}\,K(u_i+u_j+u_k)$ over a finite grid, controlled by matrix energies of the form $\operatorname{tr}P^{3/2}$.
--
--   The jump scalar constant is
--   $$
--   C_{\mathrm{jump}}=2+48\sqrt2>0 .
--   $$
--   It is the numerical factor in the bound for the change of the star energies when a single entry of the edge $0$ of the triangle array is switched on or off. That change is at most a constant times the entry's cubic mass plus a slicing term. The constant depends on nothing else.
